# Keep pull requests mergeable

Cloud Agent VMs for this repo often boot with a stale local `main` (prebuilt snapshot reuse). Opening a PR from that tip is why new PRs show merge conflicts against GitHub `main`.

## Before creating a feature branch

1. Run `git fetch origin main`.
2. Branch from `origin/main`, not from the local `main` ref:

```bash
git checkout -b cursor/<descriptive-name> origin/main
```

3. If you are already on a feature branch created from stale `main`, run `scripts/sync-with-main.sh` before editing.

## Before opening or updating a PR

1. Run `scripts/sync-with-main.sh`.
2. If it reports conflicts, resolve them, commit, and push.
3. Do not open or update a PR while it would be `CONFLICTING` against `origin/main`.

## Reduce repeat conflicts

Prefer editing a shared script (`site-preferences.js`, `assets/nav-translations.js`, `assets/nav-rail.js`) instead of copy-pasting the same navbar, language `<option>` list, or login popup into every HTML page.
